From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:25:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 33/40] Metal diamond engine: UPML a z-vector at a time for
 boxes with every z line (snapshot cg30f)

The x and y slabs of the UPML have every z line, so their cells fill whole z-vectors: one loop pass now updates a
float4 of one component (the same operations per lane; the lanes past the last z line keep their values), with one
index per component and z-vector into a table of the distinct groups of four coefficient sets, and the flux as
float4 (OPENEMS_DIAMOND_PML4=0: a float at a time). The tables are built before the kernel is compiled; the indices
are 16 bits wide when the tables allow. On a cube with a 10-cell PML on six faces the engine ran 36 % faster at
1 M cells and 17 % at 8 M with it than without (paired rounds, loaded machine); the notch tutorial gained about a
quarter. diamond_check.sh 72 of 72 identical; the probes equal the multithreaded engine's with OPENEMS_FTZ=1.

Generated-by: Claude Fable 5.2 (Anthropic)
